   548          // the follow"; circle-add/circle-remove write circles.memberDids, circle-list reads it back. The daemon
   549          // reaches this face's `circles-<tag>` by ACCESS off the catalog registry — access≠load, write-
   550          // then-sync. The circles doc rides the PRIVATE tier: the self-slot FLEET-syncs it same-operator (so a follow
   551          // lands on ALL the operator's own devices) and the DeterministicFederationGate NEVER volunteers it to a
   552          // cross-operator (the circles doc sits outside its federatable set). A follow writes ONLY the circles doc — no board shore
   553          // is reachable here, the never-federates wall made structural. `ctx.tw5` lets a mutation/list re-render
   554          // the daemon follow surface (a browser paints it; a headless node daemon rests the temp tiddler).
   555          if (ctx.oracleUrl) {
   556            // The registry a FACE's planes answer to — the persona, circles, identities, sessions and intents planes all share one
   557            // tag and one home. Built once so the two verb families below cannot drift onto different planes.
   558            const facePlane = ctx.catalogUrl ? makeCatalogAccessor(ctx.repo, ctx.catalogUrl) : null;
   559            // THE FOLLOW GRAPH BELONGS TO THE FACE THAT IS WORN, AND A FACE'S PLANES ARE USER BAGS.
   560            //
   561            // `circles-<tag>` names this PersonaGroup's own circles, derived off the same tag as its persona
   562            // plane, so a vessel holding a multitude reads the circles of the face it stands in and never
   563            // another's. The tag comes from the plane id itself — the name is the index — so nothing here holds
   564            // a second copy to drift from.
   565            //
   566            // It resolves from the catalog registry, beside the persona plane it shares a tag with: the oracle plane names the SYSTEM
   567            // bags, the universal floor every vessel carries, and a person's relations are not universal. Which
   568            // registry a face's planes answer to reads as an OWNERSHIP question rather than a measured one — the
   569            // pair matches wherever both halves are written, so evidence alone never settled it (canon:
   570            // wiki-layer-ontology, ruled by the operator).
   571            const resolveCirclesStore = async () => {
   572              const face = personaSiblingBagIds(personaBagIdFor(faceGroup()));
   573              if (!face) throw new Error("circle-verb: this vessel's PersonaGroup plane names no face");
   574              if (!facePlane) throw new Error("circle-verb: this island carries no catalog plane — a user bag has no registry to resolve from");
   575              const store = await facePlane.storeOf(face.circles);
   576              if (!store) throw new Error(`circle-verb: ${face.circles} unresolved — the catalog registry names no such plane for the face this vessel wears`);
   577              return store;
   578            };
