   632            // `face-join` — the CAPABILITY half of joining this operator's own face, run where the booted
   633            // provider already lives. A device-admit confers STANDING (a signed edge the joinee pins); keyhive
   634            // still knows no such member, so the joinee reaches the plaintext planes and decrypts nothing sealed.
   635            // A joinee summons here with its ContactCard + the edge that licenses it, and leaves holding the
   636            // group key. The human confers standing once, by hand; the machine completes the capability.
